cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this ultra-low-latency traffic shaping engine in your infrastructure research or production systems, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - given-names: "Eklavya"
    family-names: "Saini"
    alias: "Coolcubercoder"
    website: "https://github.com"
title: "Sluice: A Zero-Allocation, Multi-Tenant Atomic Token Bucket Rate Limiter in Pure Go"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-07
url: "https://github.com/sluice"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sluice"
abstract: >-
  Sluice is a high-throughput, standalone traffic-shaping library engineered to eliminate
  the 'noisy neighbor' bottleneck in hyperscale multi-tenant cloud architectures. By bypassing
  the Go runtime heap via native system call allocations and utilizing a completely lock-free,
  cache-line-isolated atomic token bucket registry, Sluice executes multi-tenant rate limiting
  at bare-metal memory speeds with absolute zero Garbage Collection overhead.
keywords:
  - golang
  - rate-limiting
  - lock-free
  - atomic
  - off-heap
  - zero-allocation
  - low-latency
  - cloud-infrastructure
license: MIT
